 @coffee7180 DLSS4 is objectively better. With that said FSR4 is at the point where it’s “good enough” for most people. 

I still think if you can get your hands on a used/refurb 3090 ti, 4070 ti, 4070 ti super, or 4080 for around the same price that’s the better option. (Due to DLSS4 support and RT performance.)

If you don’t care about FSR/RT the 9070 XT is a no brainer.

 @gorky_vk  It's not just old games, it's what you're playing RIGHT NOW, but a ton of those "old" games are still rough to run in 4k especially when you start cranking up settings and RT. That library DOES matter or were you AMD fans lying saying no one should care about RT because no games support it yet? That's a BS fanboy argument and you know it.

When every RTX owner of the last 8yrs can already utilize DLSS4 FSR4 means nothing to them, they don't have to buy a 5070ti/9070xt to use it cause they already have it. While it IS a win for those looking to get a 9070 series, DLSS is still available in FAR more games than FSR, as well as only FSR3.1 and above can be upgraded to this. With AMD's ever shrinking market share I expect that trend to continue unless AMD can REALLY move a ton of these cards. The fact we're seeing almost none at MSRP and most of them are already jacked up by hundreds I don't see that happening and most will just wait for the scalping to end and buy Nvidia anyways. 

AMD really should have priced these at $500 when it uses a similar die and memory to the 7800xt that sold for well under $500, but obviously "aggressive pricing to go after market share" was an utter lie. That lie is what disappoints me so much with RDNA4.

@gorky_vk Your reading comprehension sucks. ALL RTX users can utilize DLSS4 which allows you to use performance mode and push a lot of lower end cards into respectable 1440 and 4k territory without sacrificing fidelity. That's exactly why this is a huge middle finger to RDNA3 owners. 

If you have to cherry pick only 4080 hardware your argument is a joke. There's a shitload of AAA games RIGHT NOW that 3060 up to 4070s struggle with that can utilize DLSS4 to either enable 4k or RT at 1440 because performance mode IS viable now. Even at 1080p.

On the upgradability front AMD themselves said games on 3.1 could be upgraded to FSR4, but it needed support from the developer side, so your driver level claim is BS too. So who's telling the truth and who has no idea WTF they're talking about? You or the company that literally makes the hardware?

 @torradasuprema395  Not true for NVidia users:- I have a now-old 3080_10G... I use DLSS Transformer model at performance on 1440p...  DLSS4 Transformer in performance mode is comparable to DLSS CNN at quality mode...  

I'd be interested to see more comparisons of FSR4, BUT, I am impressed with the improvement shown here!...  

I'm not yet in the market for a new GPU, but probably by the 10070xt and 6070ti equivalent, I might be finally compelled to go AMD again.  (even more so if they do a 10080xt - the 70 series don't quite do it for me... I'm not rich enough for a xx90, but the "best of the rest", yes.)

