 @MarikoRawralton  Good point. FSR had been getting a lot of hate for its lower image quality relative to DLSS and even XeSS. Also puts more colour on AMD buying Xilinx and introducing Xilinx AI accelerators into RDNA 3.

I just hope, they are able to get FSR 4 working on RDNA 3 as well or roll out the first UDNA within a year like they did the last time they took a break from the high end between RDNA and RDNA 2. Just my nobody random internet person opinion, but as things currently stand with where the RX 9070XT and RX 9070 fall, there is little reason for people with RX 7900 XT(X) or even GRE to move to RDNA 4. Not even in ray tracing when you look at actual frame rates not the percentage change. 25% may seem like a huge change, but in practical terms it's simply 5fps when you're going from 20fps to 25fps. Even a 40% improvement is going from 20fps to 28fps. Not really worth the effort to switch if you got the higher end RDNA 3 cards. But I also get that RDNA 4 is a stop gap to UDNA so wouldn't have made sense to waste wafers on high end which is a small market segment.

Hope their pricing and the performance of these cards helps them persuade people on older GPUs to upgrade to RDNA 4 as they move to UDNA. Let's just hope that a sizeable portion of the GPUs are at MSRP throughout the life of RDNA 4. Heard rumours of incoming $800 RX 9070XT cards

 @ghiles61354  FSR and DLSS are both abundant but as we know FSR can run on anything with a third party app or as you’ve tried to detract, a mod. It makes no difference to the user nor to the game nor to FSR whether checkbox is in-game, in a third party app or in an AMD Window. It’s pretty rich to negate the distinction as anything other than better that it can run anywhere on anything, because with DLSS you’re relying not only on the developer but also your artificially software locked features on older RTX cards. 
In my experience FSR has been visually better with similar, usually slightly worse but sometimes much better performance. FSR is without the weird artefacts from oblique patters things like floor tiles. On a 3070 Ti I’ve had DLSS be so muddy and awful it’s unusable in one game, where maybe this makes it clear to you now, I’m relying on the developer or Nvidia to resolve it if ever. 
FSR on that same game works flawlessly, and it would work flawlessly whether the developer included it or not (they did), and I don’t need a special card to run it. Quit schmoozing. Open standards are better standards.

