4k DLSS performance doesnt run as good as 1080p before. Now it runs worse. So I wouldn't be surprised if 1440p native runs better and looks better than these new transformer models and FSR4

 @Struct.3 What remains to be seen is whether AMD’s offerings remain in stock at good prices and whether Nvidia’s offerings remain out of stock and overpriced.

Unfortunately the conversation isnt’t just about performance anymore, it’s also about how much we get ripped off by Nvidia.

This could turn into an actual slam dunk if the prices stay significantly in AMD’s advantage. 5080 and 5090 are waaayyyy too expensive for the vast majority of users.

 @KevinFought  You're arguing semantics and being obtuse, which is not helpful to the overall conversation. It may not be exactly by definition a monopoly, but for all intents and purposes, Nvidia has a near monopoly on discrete GPUs.

It is true that they are making superior products, but Nvidia, like every other company, wants to maximize their profits, and them holding such power in the market allows them to get away with pricing that is unheard of.

And that is the essence of the OG claim, that we need more actuall meaningful competition so the users can benefit. Not the kind of surface level competition that just allows us to say "well actually Nvidia is not a monopoly because competition exists".

